WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.090
2018's blockbuster season is officially underway.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.050
The months ahead will see the release of plenty
of high profile titles, including Deadpool

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:13.300
2, Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom, and Solo:
A Star Wars Story, and that's just the beginning.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:17.570
In fact, just about every major upcoming film
dropped a new trailer over the past month.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.090
It's a lot to take in if you're not paying
attention.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.019
In case you missed them, here's a look at
all the new trailers from April 2018 that

00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:26.189
are sure to blow you away.

00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:27.189
The Cleanse

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:30.990
Not to be confused with the movie The Purge,
The Cleanse sees a group of people heading

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.180
out to a mountain health retreat to partake
in a purging ritual to cleanse the toxins

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.180
from their body.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.400
But one guy purges something a little more
sinister than bad feelings: He lets out an

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.760
actual demon.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.550
The Cleanse premiered at South by Southwest
in 2016 under the title The Master Cleanse,

00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:49.550
then sat quietly for two years waiting for
a distribution deal.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.490
With a brand new trailer preceding the film's
upcoming release, mainstream audiences finally

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:55.640
got a glimpse of the quirky horror comedy.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.330
Look for The Cleanse in theaters and on video-on-demand
on May 4th.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.410
The 12th Man

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:04.750
This upcoming film tells the true story of
a Norwegian freedom fighter who goes on the

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.979
run after his group of saboteurs is captured
and executed by the Nazis.

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:13.549
Equal parts harrowing survival thriller and
action-packed war drama, The 12th Man is bound

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:15.520
to be a tense, unforgettable experience.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.609
While the film premiered in Norway in December
2017, distributor IFC Midnight has it slated

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:23.179
for a May 4th release in the U.S.

00:01:23.179 --> 00:01:24.179
Anon

00:01:24.179 --> 00:01:28.320
From writer/director Andrew Niccol, Anon takes
place in the near future where surveillance

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.450
technology ensures that nothing happens without
a record.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:34.119
Everything a person sees is recorded and archived.

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:37.060
Anonymity is a thing of the past, and no crime
goes unpunished.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.679
But when Detective Sal Freiland played by
Clive Owen, encounters a mysterious woman

00:01:41.679 --> 00:01:46.709
who can erase all records of her existence,
he finds himself plunged into a world of paranoia

00:01:46.709 --> 00:01:48.840
where nothing is what it seems.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:52.189
Look for Anon on Netflix on May 4th.

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:53.490
Deadpool 2

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.399
Fox was more than happy to let the fan speculation
about the new mutants in Deadpool 2 run wild

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:02.920
for months, but their final trailer finally
names a few of the newcomers, like Bedlam

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:03.920
and Shatterstar.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.289
Oh, and Peter, who just wants to hang out.

00:02:06.289 --> 00:02:08.820
"Um, I just saw the ad."

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:10.360
"You're in."

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.900
What else is there to see in the newest Deadpool
2 trailer?

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.990
A whole lot of action and plenty of jokes,
of course.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.250
"So dark.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:19.320
You sure you're not from the DC universe?"

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.690
Deadpool 2 lands in theaters on May 18th.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.690
Cargo

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:28.030
Starring Martin Freeman, Cargo tells the story
of a father in rural Australia who finds himself

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:30.440
stranded in the middle of a zombie outbreak.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.340
To make matters worse, he's stuck with the
most precious cargo of all, his infant daughter.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:39.920
Based on a short film that made waves at Tropfest
Australia in 2013, Cargo sees the original

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.400
short's directors behind the camera for the
feature-length adaptation.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.500
With a brand new trailer released in April,
Netflix offers a glimpse of the desolate world

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.870
of Cargo and promises an emotionally charged
journey with the ultimate stakes.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.599
Look for it on May 18th.

00:02:53.599 --> 00:02:56.099
Solo: A Star Wars Story

00:02:56.099 --> 00:03:00.310
In a world where expensive blockbusters always
seem to want to bet on a sure thing, a Han

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.860
Solo origin story was all but inevitable.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:07.760
The new trailer for Solo: A Star Wars story
sees Alden Ehrenreich's young Han taking on

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.140
what looks like his first smuggling job.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.530
He's joined by Chewbacca, and for once, maybe
even the last time in his life, he has a good

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.040
feeling about things.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.860
Unfortunately, most fans aren't feeling so
good about it.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.590
Between a change of directors at the last
minute and reports of Disney bringing in an

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:26.370
acting coach for Ehrenreich, things haven't
boded well for this new incarnation of the

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.370
scruffy nerf-herder.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:33.000
We'll all have to see what happens in this
galaxy far, far, away on May 25th.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Future World

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.000
Bizarre.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Strange.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Inexplicable.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.970
There are many words to describe the trailer
for Future World, but they all basically mean

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:40.989
the same thing.

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:47.060
James Franco stars as a weird post-apocalyptic
warlord, with Suki Waterhouse as a weird robot,

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:52.650
Milla Jovovich as a weirder version of Resident
Evil's Alice, and Snoop Dogg as, well...he's

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.080
pretty normal, all things considered.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.819
"You say that like that's a bad thing or something,
man."

00:03:56.819 --> 00:03:59.439
The trailer is full of this stuff, and more.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:03.410
Future World probably won't win any awards,
but it looks like a fun ride for anyone craving

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.900
some sci-fi action.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:09.000
Look for Future World to drop on video-on-demand
on May 25th.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.000
Upgrade

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.500
Upcoming action extravaganza Upgrade stars
Logan Marshall-Green as a regular ol' guy

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.940
who gets a neural implant that turns him into
a human weapon.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:22.300
Is it the easiest writing trick in the world
to give your protagonist super fighting skills?

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.740
You bet, but from the looks of the trailer,
Upgrade will have more than enough style to

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.980
pull it off.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.000
Whether any of that translates into a good
movie remains to be seen, but we'll be able

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.220
to find out when Upgrade hits theaters on
June 1st.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.639
American Animals

00:04:35.639 --> 00:04:40.419
Evan Peters headlines American Animals as
the real-life Warren Lipka, a college student

00:04:40.419 --> 00:04:44.710
who orchestrated a bizarre heist to steal
a collection of rare books from the library

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:47.380
at Kentucky's Transylvania University.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:51.539
Together with three friends, Lipka carried
out a meticulous plan to infiltrate the Rare

00:04:51.539 --> 00:04:56.360
Book Room, subdue its one guard, a 50-year-old
librarian, and get rich by making off with

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.360
millions of dollars' worth of first editions.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.169
"Can I just say how dumb this entire thing
is?"

00:05:01.169 --> 00:05:05.779
The trailer promises a college-bound heist
movie equal parts Ocean's Eleven and Harold

00:05:05.779 --> 00:05:06.779
&amp; Kumar.

00:05:06.779 --> 00:05:09.060
Check it out on June 1st.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.180
Ocean's 8

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.789
While George Clooney's Danny Ocean was the
central driving force behind the first three

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:17.949
Oceans movies, it's his sister, Debbie Ocean,
who's putting together a team for Ocean's

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:18.949
8.

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:23.349
The heist: Steal a priceless diamond necklace
from the New York Met Gala.

00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:26.270
The plan: super convoluted, as usual.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:29.970
Sandra Bullock leads an all-star cast, and
Steven Soderbergh, who directed the first

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.880
three films, serves as a producer.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:37.060
Look for all the high-stakes heist action
when Ocean's 8 lands in theaters on June 8th.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.289
Hereditary

00:05:38.289 --> 00:05:43.310
The first trailer for A24's Hereditary promised
a visually unique horror tale centered around

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:45.300
an unsettling young girl named Charlie.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:49.850
In the second trailer, Charlie's inner demons
crawl into the light just a little bit more.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:53.160
It still doesn't explain much about the story,
but it doesn't need to.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:57.229
The trailer is a whirlwind of activity, and
if the movie is even half as creepy as these

00:05:57.229 --> 00:06:01.380
trailers have been, it's bound to become one
of the best horror films of 2018.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.960
You can find out when it hits theaters on
June 8th.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.099
Hotel Artemis

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:10.150
The April trailer for Hotel Artemis dropped
out of a clear blue sky, but was quick to

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:14.050
pull in millions of views...and plenty of
comparisons to John Wick.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:18.810
Hotel Artemis is about a hospital for assassins
that accepts the wrong patient, drawing in

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:21.759
the underworld's deadliest like moths to a
lamp.

00:06:21.759 --> 00:06:27.590
Hotel Artemis is a no-vacancy, no-holds-barred
mashup of slick action and all-star faces.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.520
Look for it in theaters on June 8th.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:31.770
Incredibles 2

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:35.450
After 14 years of waiting, Incredibles 2 is
finally on the way.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:39.300
Original writer/director Brad Bird is helming
the sequel, with most the of the original

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.870
voice cast back as well.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:44.879
The timing couldn't be more perfect to rope
in all those fans of the first film, plus

00:06:44.879 --> 00:06:45.940
their kids.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:49.750
The new trailer sees Elastigirl heading out
to fight crime, leaving Mr. Incredible at

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.190
home to wrangle the kids.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:55.159
In the latter half of the trailer, we get
glimpses of the whole family in action, along

00:06:55.159 --> 00:07:00.610
with shots of the Underminer terrorizing the
city and the mysterious new villain The Screenslaver

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:02.930
brainwashing the citizens of Metroville.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.350
Check out Incredibles 2 in theaters on June
15th.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.419
Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:13.250
Universal Pictures released yet another teaser
for Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom in April,

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:16.669
building the hype even higher for a movie
that millions of people are going to go see

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:17.669
anyway.

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:21.819
In the final full-length trailer, Universal
finally gets down to brass tacks, storywise.

00:07:21.819 --> 00:07:25.830
Claire and Owen are heading back to the island
to rescue the dinosaurs from a volcano, but

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:31.009
the corporation that sends them isn't interested
in happy dinos, they want to use Owen's velociraptor,

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:35.360
Blue, to make a new hybrid weapon and auction
it off to the highest bidder.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.450
Nobody's taking bets on whether anything goes
wrong with that plan.

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:42.220
Look for Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom in
theaters on June 22nd.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.940
The First Purge

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.580
You've seen three years of the Purge, now
get ready for the one that started it all.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.550
There are some serious shenanigans at work
in the trailer for The First Purge, with the

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:55.230
government enlisting black ops soldiers to
help get the ball rolling on the first night

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:56.230
of their new experiment.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:59.750
Turns out, people aren't so keen to go on
those bloody rampages after all.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.509
"I can't run around chopping people's heads
off one day a year, and then sleep well the

00:08:03.509 --> 00:08:04.509
rest of the time."

00:08:04.509 --> 00:08:07.340
"Well you better start getting used to it,
little bitch, because we've got some f---ing

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:08.340
company."

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.960
Writer and director James DeMonaco, who helmed
the first three Purge films, returns as the

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:16.980
writer on The First Purge, with Gerard McMurray
stepping in as director.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:20.509
The First Purge drops into theaters on July
4th.

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:22.330
The Equalizer 2

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:27.699
In this sequel to 2014's The Equalizer, Denzel
Washington returns as Robert McCall, the ultimate

00:08:27.699 --> 00:08:30.409
man of peace who you definitely don't want
to mess with.

00:08:30.409 --> 00:08:34.599
The trailer showcases Washington going on
a rampage while keeping plot details pretty

00:08:34.599 --> 00:08:39.800
much under wraps, promising an adrenaline-fueled
ride packed with plenty of surprises.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:44.000
Check it out when The Equalizer 2 turns up
the heat on July 20th.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Night School

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:49.430
In a summer filled to the brim with monster
films, superhero smackdowns, and spine-tingling

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:52.430
horror, Night School is bound to be a breath
of fresh air.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:56.810
The comedy stars Kevin Hart as a successful
grill salesman whose life is flipped upside

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:59.030
down when his store blows up.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:02.450
When nobody will hire him because he's a high-school
dropout, he suddenly finds himself at the

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:06.360
bottom of the corporate ladder, enrolling
in night school to get his G.E.D.

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:10.390
With a script co-written by Kevin Hart, Night
School co-stars Tiffany Haddish and enrolls

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.590
in a theater near you on September 28th.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:14.590
The Meg

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:19.810
Throughout his career, Jason Statham has gone
up against gypsies, human traffickers, '80s

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.370
action stars, and his own heart.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.740
Now, he's facing his biggest foe yet, a prehistoric
sea monster.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:30.410
The Meg sees Statham starring as Jonas Taylor,
an ex-Navy Captain who's recruited to help

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.440
with a rescue mission on a deep-sea research
station.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.320
The only problem is, there's a 70-foot predator
roaming the seas.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:41.550
In the first trailer for The Meg, we get some
underwater action, some explosions, and at

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:46.180
least one too many jokes about how there's
no way this Megalodon's actually a Megalodon,

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.370
even though it's clearly a Megalodon.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.840
"It's a Megalodon."

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:52.350
"He's kidding, right?"

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:56.100
Take the plunge when The Meg arrives on August
10th.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.100
Venom

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:00.760
After teasing the world with a Venom trailer
that didn't feature any Venom, Sony finally

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:03.450
released a trailer chock-full of the symbiote.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.990
The teaser introduces Tom Hardy's character,
Eddie Brock, a reporter digging into a story

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:11.950
involving a shadowy tech company called the
Life Foundation that's apparently been attempting

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:14.070
to merge people with symbiotes.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:18.200
When Brock gets infected with a symbiote,
the Life Foundation's Dr. Carlton Drake sends

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:22.279
his henchmen after the guy, and they end up
getting more than they bargained for.

00:10:22.279 --> 00:10:26.320
Another highlight of the new trailer is the
introduction of Venom's voice, also voiced

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.340
by Hardy.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:30.200
Look for Venom to hit theaters on October
5th.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.410
The Man Who Killed Don Quixote

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:37.130
It took almost 20 years for Terry Gilliam
to bring his passion project about Don Quixote

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:41.230
to fruition, and the long journey is finally,
almost, over.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:45.240
The original incarnation starred Johnny Depp,
but a long, troubled production eventually

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.730
sucked the funding out of the movie, and everyone
went their separate ways.

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:53.850
After multiple restarts, misfires, and casting
replacements, the film now stars Adam Driver,

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:56.390
with Jonathan Pryce as Don Quixote.

00:10:56.390 --> 00:11:00.880
And believe it or not, the Don Quixote curse
has struck again, as of April 2018, Gilliam

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.170
is still embroiled in a legal battle over
the new film's distribution rights.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:09.070
Fingers crossed that all those troubles come
to an end and The Man Who Killed Don Quixote

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.980
finally reaches theaters.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.370
Thanks for watching!

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:15.000
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.410
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

